Here is a correct example of the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm:
```python
def find_majority_element(arr):
    count = 0
    candidate = None
    for num in arr:
        if count == 0:
            candidate = num
        count += (1 if num == candidate else -1)
    return candidate
```
This implementation has a time complexity of O(n) and accurately represents the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm.
